    <section id="faq" class="py-5">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center mb-4">
          <div class="text-uppercase small text-secondary fw-semibold mb-2">FAQ</div>
          <h2 class="section-title display-6">Common questions, answered clearly</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion accordion-flush glass-card p-3" id="faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-item bg-transparent border-0">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed bg-transparent shadow-none" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">
                <span>Are my files uploaded to a server?</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                No. Files2Zip compresses everything client-side using JavaScript. Your files never leave your browser.<br>However, if you email the ZIP file you made or save it to Dropbox, that ZIP file <em>is</em> sent to our server and saved there for a short time.              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="accordion-item bg-transparent border-0">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed bg-transparent shadow-none" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">
                <span>Is there a file size or count limit?</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                There is no artificial limit. The only constraint is your device memory: browsers can typically handle archives up to a couple of gigabytes before performance degrades.              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item bg-transparent border-0">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed bg-transparent shadow-none" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">
                <span>Why are the <em>Email</em> and <em>Dropbox</em> buttons disabled?</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                If the ZIP file you've created is larger than 100MB, we can't offer email/Dropbox integrations. You can only download the ZIP file and then process it yourself.              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

        <section id="stats" class="py-5">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center mb-4">
          <div class="text-uppercase small text-secondary fw-semibold mb-2">Statistics</div>
        </div>

        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-center gap-3 mb-4">

          <div class="stat">
              <div id="stat_archives_extracted" class="fs-1 fw-bolder">236,821</div>
              Archives extracted          </div>

          <div class="stat">
              <div id="stat_archives_created" class="fs-1 fw-bolder">201,175</div>
              Archives created          </div>

          <div class="stat">
            <div id="stat_files_created" class="fs-1 fw-bolder">66,381,575</div>
            Files extracted          </div>

          <div class="stat">
            <div id="stat_files_compressed" class="fs-1 fw-bolder">53,330,140</div>
            Files compressed          </div>

          <div class="stat">
            <div id="stat_bytes_saved" class="fs-1 fw-bolder">4.2TB</div>
            Space saved          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="small text-secondary">since July 2026</div>
      </div>

    </section>
    
  </main>

